1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Welcome back! In the last video we talked about materials and the physical laser.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Today we're going to be talking about the software side of things.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:16,000
In this video we're going to be talking about X-Tool Studio, sometimes listed as X-Tool Creative Studio.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
This is the software where you will create all of your laser designs.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,000
You are welcome to come use it at the library, but you can also download and use it from home.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:33,000
This can be particularly useful if you'd like to do some advanced design work before you come in to start running your projects.

7
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:38,000
If you do download it at home, you will be prompted to create an X-Tool account.

8
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,000
The software is still free, but it will have you create a login.

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,000
When you are at the library, we will have you be logged into and use the library account.

10
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,000
So please do not log into a personal account on the library computer.

11
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:59,000
When you are on the library computer, you should see this as your home page.

12
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:07,000
You will at the top see recently opened files. These will be files from either you or other laser users.

13
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:13,000
We do ask that you be respectful. Please don't open and begin editing other users designs.

14
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Down below that you can also see suggested designs from X-Tool.

15
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:28,000
These are going to be designs from other laser users outside of the library, but you are welcome to open and use these.

16
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:32,660
They are intended to be shared and made.

17
00:01:32,660 --> 00:01:35,660
Over here on the left side is your navigation menu.

18
00:01:35,660 --> 00:01:38,660
There are several things that you can do from here.

19
00:01:38,660 --> 00:01:41,660
The first is go to the MySpace tab.

20
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:48,660
This will be where any designs that are uploaded and saved to the shared library account end up.

21
00:01:48,660 --> 00:01:53,660
If you choose to save your design, it will be visible to other users here.

22
00:01:53,660 --> 00:01:58,660
Once you have finished your design, if you would like it to no longer be visible to other users,

23
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:03,660
you can hit the three dots in the corner of your design and hit delete.

24
00:02:03,660 --> 00:02:06,660
That will remove it from here.

25
00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:10,660
The other option right above that is the download button.

26
00:02:10,660 --> 00:02:13,660
That is going to be the easiest way to transfer files.

27
00:02:13,660 --> 00:02:19,660
If you have made a design at home that you would like to bring into the library to run,

28
00:02:19,660 --> 00:02:25,660
the easiest way to achieve that is to download it as an XCS file.

29
00:02:25,660 --> 00:02:29,660
Right here we can see XCS is our file format.

30
00:02:29,660 --> 00:02:33,660
We can save it, in this case to our downloads folder.

31
00:02:33,660 --> 00:02:40,660
You would choose to save it to a flash drive, upload it to your email, upload it to your Google Drive.

32
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:44,660
However you want to transport that file to the library.

33
00:02:44,660 --> 00:02:49,660
What you would then do is either plug your flash drive in to the library computer

34
00:02:49,660 --> 00:02:54,660
or log into your email on the library computer to download that file.

35
00:02:54,660 --> 00:02:59,660
Download it and then hit upload up here in the corner.

36
00:02:59,660 --> 00:03:03,660
From here you can select which file you are uploading.

37
00:03:03,660 --> 00:03:07,660
When we hit open, we will see that new file up here.

38
00:03:07,660 --> 00:03:11,660
In this case, we have a copy of this feather design.

39
00:03:11,660 --> 00:03:14,660
Either one of those is going to work just fine.

40
00:03:14,660 --> 00:03:17,660
I could open both of these and they would be the exact same

41
00:03:17,660 --> 00:03:21,660
and it will save things like the cut settings and things like that.

42
00:03:21,660 --> 00:03:25,660
Since we don't need two copies of that design, I am going to go ahead and delete it.

43
00:03:25,660 --> 00:03:31,300
A little further down, we have our explorer tab.

44
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:36,300
This is going to be where you can find existing designs.

45
00:03:36,300 --> 00:03:41,300
These are all going to be from other XTool users outside of the library.

46
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:46,300
This is going to be where people come to share designs that they have made.

47
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:51,670
You can either just take the homepage and see what you see

48
00:03:51,670 --> 00:03:53,670
or you can search for specific things.

49
00:03:53,670 --> 00:03:57,670
In this case, I was searching for coffee themed designs.

50
00:03:57,670 --> 00:04:02,670
You can also search for things like dinosaurs.

51
00:04:02,670 --> 00:04:08,670
If you are looking for something more practical, you can search for a desk organizer

52
00:04:08,670 --> 00:04:13,670
and find a wide variety of designs.

53
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:17,670
Once you have found a design that you like,

54
00:04:17,670 --> 00:04:22,670
let's come back and search for something basic like a nice cat.

55
00:04:22,670 --> 00:04:28,780
I think this will work really well.

56
00:04:28,780 --> 00:04:31,780
Let's go ahead and open up these cat earrings.

57
00:04:31,780 --> 00:04:36,780
When we click on that design, we can see a couple of things.

58
00:04:36,780 --> 00:04:40,780
We can see what material that they used.

59
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:44,780
We can see a preview of what the design will look like.

60
00:04:44,780 --> 00:04:50,780
We can see the user that submitted this design.

61
00:04:50,780 --> 00:04:53,780
Then we can see which machine that they used.

62
00:04:53,780 --> 00:04:57,780
In this case, since we have a P2S, we would like to see

63
00:04:57,780 --> 00:05:00,780
that listed as either the machine that they used

64
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:03,780
or here under compatible machines.

65
00:05:03,780 --> 00:05:06,780
If the P2S is not listed as a compatible machine,

66
00:05:06,780 --> 00:05:09,780
that doesn't mean your design won't work,

67
00:05:09,780 --> 00:05:12,780
but it may mean you have to do a little more converting in terms of size,

68
00:05:12,780 --> 00:05:15,780
in terms of getting the file to function,

69
00:05:15,780 --> 00:05:19,780
especially things that are made specifically for UV lasers,

70
00:05:19,780 --> 00:05:21,780
like the F2 and F1,

71
00:05:21,780 --> 00:05:26,780
may have some struggles being ported over to a CO2 laser

72
00:05:26,780 --> 00:05:28,780
like the one we use here at the library.

73
00:05:28,780 --> 00:05:31,780
You can also see the material that they used here.

74
00:05:31,780 --> 00:05:34,780
You do not have to use the same material,

75
00:05:34,780 --> 00:05:37,780
but if you would like your design to match theirs,

76
00:05:37,780 --> 00:05:40,780
you'll want to use something that looks similar.

77
00:05:40,780 --> 00:05:43,780
Then we can go ahead and hit open,

78
00:05:43,780 --> 00:05:46,780
and we can see our design pull up.

79
00:05:46,780 --> 00:05:48,780
When you are on the library account,

80
00:05:48,780 --> 00:05:51,780
you'll see the laser already connected.

81
00:05:51,780 --> 00:05:55,780
In this case, it is not because I'm recording in the studio,

82
00:05:55,780 --> 00:05:57,780
but we'll show what it looks like

83
00:05:57,780 --> 00:06:02,780
when the laser is connected a little down the line.

84
00:06:02,780 --> 00:06:04,780
But I can see my design.

85
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:08,780
I can select it and move it around if I need to.

86
00:06:08,780 --> 00:06:10,780
I can also move around specific elements,

87
00:06:10,780 --> 00:06:12,780
so I can either move all of my design

88
00:06:12,780 --> 00:06:15,780
or just specific parts to reorient them.

89
00:06:15,780 --> 00:06:18,780
Now, this is an important distinction.

90
00:06:18,780 --> 00:06:21,780
Not all designs are free.

91
00:06:21,780 --> 00:06:23,780
When you are on the library account,

92
00:06:23,780 --> 00:06:26,780
we will ask you to only utilize free designs,

93
00:06:26,780 --> 00:06:30,780
but there are paid designs here in Extool Studio.

94
00:06:30,780 --> 00:06:31,780
I'm going to turn on our filters

95
00:06:31,780 --> 00:06:34,780
so that we only see those for just a moment.

96
00:06:34,780 --> 00:06:36,780
When you see a file that is like this

97
00:06:36,780 --> 00:06:38,780
and has a price in the corner,

98
00:06:38,780 --> 00:06:40,780
that is one that we will ask you

99
00:06:40,780 --> 00:06:43,780
to not use while on the library account.

100
00:06:43,780 --> 00:06:45,780
What you can, however, do

101
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:49,780
is make this purchase on a personal device,

102
00:06:49,780 --> 00:06:52,780
so on your own computer, on your own cell phone,

103
00:06:52,780 --> 00:06:57,060
log into a personal account,

104
00:06:57,060 --> 00:06:59,060
click on one of these designs,

105
00:06:59,060 --> 00:07:00,060
and once you purchase it,

106
00:07:00,060 --> 00:07:05,060
it will provide you the file as an XCS format.

107
00:07:05,060 --> 00:07:07,060
XCSes are transferable,

108
00:07:07,060 --> 00:07:10,060
so once you have purchased it on a personal device,

109
00:07:10,060 --> 00:07:13,060
you can, just like we talked about before,

110
00:07:13,060 --> 00:07:16,060
place it on a flash drive or email it to yourself

111
00:07:16,060 --> 00:07:20,060
and then open that already paid for file

112
00:07:20,060 --> 00:07:22,060
here on the library account.

113
00:07:22,060 --> 00:07:26,060
In the next video, we'll take a little more

114
00:07:26,060 --> 00:07:29,060
in-depth look at our earring design here

115
00:07:29,060 --> 00:07:32,060
and the software side of things.

116
00:07:32,060 --> 00:07:34,060
We'll talk about how to edit a design

117
00:07:34,060 --> 00:07:37,060
or create a design from scratch

118
00:07:37,060 --> 00:07:41,060
and how to use some of the tools here in the canvas.
